.task-board/.resources/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:5731:[{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records device and OS, source and dependency revisions, config, traffic, duration, flow counts, physical footprint, peak, available-memory samples, sessions, buffers, queued bytes, descriptors, tasks, drops, and failures. 2. Staged counts stop at the measured safe ceiling with an explicit reason; the task does not force 1200 sessions when the device budget rejects it. 3. At least one hundred start and stop cycles plus cancellation at multiple startup points show no monotonic descriptor, task, session, or physical-footprint growth. 4. Soft, pressure, and critical simulations verify the spike can reduce or stop work in the specified order or explicitly identify behavior deferred until SSH integration. 5. The report states whether the 25–30 MiB steady-state target is met, the remaining budget for SSH, DNS, relay, caches, and reconnect overlap, and every unresolved risk.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-35wctc","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2jatnd"],"checklist":[{"text":"Staged concurrency and lifecycle rows stop at measured safe limits","done":false},{"text":"Physical footprint, available memory, sessions, descriptors, tasks, and drops are recorded","done":false},{"text":"Budget analysis and reproducible raw evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:37Z","description":"Measure the full bridge and HEV baseline under staged flow counts, repeated provider lifecycle, cancellation, and pressure on the physical iPhone and Mac. Establish whether the provisional 25–30 MiB extension target and bounded resource contract are credible.","id":"TASK-260715-135rr8","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-physical-memory-lifecycle-and-concurrency-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: staged 100, 250, 500, and measured configuration-limit flows; many idle connections; mixed bidirectional traffic; start and stop loops; cancellation during start; host termination; sleep and wake where supported by the spike; induced memory pressure; physical footprint and peak; os_proc_available_memory samples; HEV sessions; socket buffers; queued bytes; descriptors; tasks; counters; reconnect-overlap estimate. Out of scope: claiming an Apple memory guarantee, SSH channel allocations not yet implemented, production reconnect, jetsam experimentation that risks device stability, and raising limits to hit an arbitrary count.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the physical memory, lifecycle, and concurrency matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. The exact pinned HEV sources build and link through the approved native packaging seam for macOS harness, macOS provider, iOS simulator, and iOS device configurations. 2. HEV receives only the bridge-owned endpoint and starts with the recorded MTU and exact UDP-in-TCP and low-memory configuration values. 3. The internal SOCKS endpoint is process-local or otherwise cryptographically or structurally restricted to the owned adapter path and rejects an external ingress test. 4. Startup failure and cancellation close HEV tasks, the transferred descriptor, listener state, and bridge resources without double close. 5. Required HEV, core, task-system, and lwIP notices are present in produced test bundles and trace to the pinned manifest.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-uopycx","TASK-260715-3o0co4","TASK-260715-1g9cyt"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-35wctc","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"checklist":[{"text":"Pinned unmodified HEV builds in harness and all Apple target configurations","done":false},{"text":"Fixed configuration and owned SOCKS boundary are enforced","done":false},{"text":"Lifecycle, linkage, and notice evidence is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:35Z","description":"Build the pinned unmodified HEV stack for the harness and both Apple provider configurations, hand it the owned socket-pair endpoint, apply the fixed UDP-in-TCP and low-memory baseline, and expose its process-local SOCKS side to an injectable adapter seam.","id":"TASK-260715-1vv52g","isBlocked":true,"name":"integrate-unmodified-hev-lwip-with-bridge","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: reproducible HEV builds; descriptor handoff; config generation; MTU input; socks5.udp tcp; task-stack-size 24576; tcp-buffer-size 4096; max-session-count 1200 baseline; process-local SOCKS listener or owned channel; startup health; coordinated shutdown; metrics and notice bundling. Out of scope: SSHProxyAdapter implementation, final memory constants, remote relay, fork patches, production routes and DNS, and acceptance of external SOCKS clients.","status":"backlog","title":"Integrate unmodified HEV and lwIP with the bridge","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped ADR links every required M0 Bridge row to reproducible evidence and marks pass, fail, or blocked without averaging away a red platform or address-family result. 2. The record selects initial MTU, requested socket buffers, batch count and time budgets, HEV settings, and measured session ceiling with rationale. 3. Pass requires public API only, correct IPv4 and IPv6 framing, bounded backpressure, clean lifecycle, no nominal unexplained loss, and physical-device memory headroom. 4. A fork is rejected by default and allowed only when Instruments identifies bridge copies or syscalls as a material bottleneck and a measured callback prototype improves it with regression coverage and rebase plan. 5. Residual risks, device and OS revalidation triggers, notices, and tasks unblocked for M1 are explicit.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-gyg51r","TASK-260715-135rr8"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2xx2tk"],"checklist":[{"text":"Every M0 Bridge gate row traces to reproducible evidence","done":false},{"text":"Configuration and memory baselines are selected without weakening red rows","done":false},{"text":"The fork disposition and TASK-ID-scoped ADR are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:37Z","description":"Consolidate implementation, deterministic tests, fuzzing, physical MTU, pressure, lifecycle, and memory evidence into the M0 Bridge gate decision, including initial configuration and the measured fork-versus-upstream disposition.","id":"TASK-260715-2jatnd","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-m0-packet-bridge-decision","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: public-API compliance; correctness; selected MTU, socket buffers, batch budgets, and session baseline; error and drop behavior; physical-device memory headroom; known gaps; upstream pin; notice status; fork decision; revalidation triggers; downstream M1 readiness. Out of scope: SSH or relay gate claims, production route and DNS approval, future performance guarantees, and authorizing a fork without Instruments evidence.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the M0 packet-bridge and HEV decision","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. Deterministic integration tests complete IPv4 and IPv6 TCP handshake, bidirectional stream, half-close, reset, and independent concurrent-flow scenarios through the real HEV binary. 2. The adapter fixture observes the expected SOCKS CONNECT and UDP-in-TCP contract, and an unowned client cannot use the internal endpoint. 3. Receiver stalls cause only bounded socket drops and recorded counters; no unbounded application queue appears. 4. Configuration tests prove the requested MTU and fixed low-memory and UDP settings reach HEV. 5. At least one hundred harness start, traffic, and stop cycles return tasks, descriptors, sessions, and allocated test resources to baseline.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3dn813","TASK-260715-1vv52g"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-gyg51r","TASK-260715-135rr8"],"checklist":[{"text":"Real HEV integration covers IPv4, IPv6, stream lifecycle, and SOCKS framing","done":false},{"text":"Stall and repeated lifecycle behavior remains bounded","done":false},{"text":"Integration test matrix and passing evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:36Z","description":"Exercise the real unmodified HEV stack through PacketFlowBridge in the macOS harness and Apple-provider test seams, proving IPv4 and IPv6 TCP translation, SOCKS contract behavior, configuration, backpressure propagation, and clean lifecycle before physical performance runs.","id":"TASK-260715-35wctc","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-hev-bridge-integration-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: real HEV and lwIP; synthetic packet endpoints; local SOCKS adapter fixture; IPv4 and IPv6 TCP handshakes and streams; half-close and reset; mixed small and bulk flows; UDP-in-TCP request framing exposure; internal endpoint rejection; induced stalls; startup and stop loops; observable counters. Out of scope: real SSH, remote UDP relay, default routes, system DNS, production internet destinations, and final throughput claims.","status":"backlog","title":"Add HEV bridge integration tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. Swift Testing cases cover forward and reverse IPv4 and IPv6 framing byte-for-byte and prove malformed or unknown frames are dropped with the correct counter. 2. Deterministic fault injection proves each bounded-drop errno, fatal EMSGSIZE metadata, persistent-error transition, and no retry or side-buffer behavior. 3. Batch-count and fake-clock time budgets stop work predictably and yield to other tasks. 4. Cancellation at every startup stage and at least one hundred start and stop cycles leave descriptor, task, and continuation counts at baseline. 5. Tests assert metric names, units, monotonic counters, effective buffer values, and maximum observed datagram size.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3o0co4"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-35wctc"],"checklist":[{"text":"Swift Testing covers every framing and errno branch deterministically","done":false},{"text":"Cancellation and repeated lifecycle return all tracked resources to baseline","done":false},{"text":"Test inventory and passing evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:35Z","description":"Create deterministic Swift Testing coverage for packet framing, batching, socket limits, backpressure, errors, cancellation, and resource cleanup using injected packet-flow, socket, clock, and fault controls.","id":"TASK-260715-3dn813","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-packet-flow-bridge-unit-and-fault-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: IPv4 and IPv6 family headers; endianness; empty, undersized, unknown-family, and oversized frames; packet boundaries; batch count and time budgets; effective-buffer readback; induced EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, ENOBUFS, EMSGSIZE, persistent errors, cancellation races, partial startup, repeated lifecycle, and descriptor accounting. Out of scope: HEV behavior, physical-device throughput, SSH, route or DNS integration, and tests that depend on arbitrary sleeps.","status":"backlog","title":"Add PacketFlowBridge unit and fault-injection tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. Static inspection and tests show that the implementation references only NEPacketTunnelFlow and documented Darwin socket APIs and never discovers or reopens utun descriptors. 2. Each packet read from packetFlow is sent as one datagram with the correct family header, and each valid reverse datagram becomes one packet with the matching protocol family. 3. Socket buffer requests and effective readbacks are exposed in metrics; EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, and ENOBUFS increment distinct drop counters without retry or side storage. 4. EMSGSIZE fails the current start with attempted datagram size and effective limit; persistent failures produce bounded privacy-safe errors. 5. All descriptors, read sources, continuations, and tasks close exactly once under normal stop, start failure, and cancellation.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-p89bdj","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-pmww4f"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3dn813","TASK-260715-1vv52g","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"checklist":[{"text":"Bridge implementation follows the approved public-API and ownership contract","done":false},{"text":"Backpressure, EMSGSIZE, metrics, and bounded batching are implemented","done":false},{"text":"Implementation notes and verification commands are attached as a TASK-ID-scoped outcome","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:35Z","description":"Implement the Swift bridge that exchanges packet batches between NEPacketTunnelFlow and the HEV descriptor endpoint through a nonblocking AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM socket pair, following the approved contract exactly.","id":"TASK-260715-3o0co4","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-public-socket-pair-packet-flow-bridge","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: socket-pair creation; close-on-exec and nonblocking configuration; socket-buffer request and effective-value readback; endpoint transfer; four-byte network-order AF_INET and AF_INET6 headers; batch reads and writes; count and time budgets; reason-specific counters; cancellation; privacy-safe failures; dependency injection. Out of scope: HEV startup, SSH, routes, DNS, private APIs, retries after bounded-queue drops, unbounded buffering, final tuning constants, and product UI.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement the public socket-pair PacketFlowBridge","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. The fuzz target or deterministic Swift property harness accepts arbitrary bytes and never reads beyond frame boundaries or allocates relative to an untrusted declared length beyond the configured datagram ceiling. 2. Seed corpus covers IPv4, IPv6, empty, 1–3 byte, unknown-family, exact MTU, over-MTU, and prior regression cases. 3. CI runs a bounded deterministic corpus; a documented extended command records seed, duration, iterations, peak allocation, and source revision. 4. Any crash or invariant violation produces a minimized replay fixture and concrete bug before this task can pass. 5. Passing evidence demonstrates bounded runtime and memory for the configured corpus and asserts reason-specific malformed counters.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3o0co4","TASK-260715-1vv52g"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-gyg51r","TASK-260715-135rr8"],"checklist":[{"text":"Arbitrary frame input is bounded by explicit length, allocation, and runtime ceilings","done":false},{"text":"Seed and regression corpus is replayable in CI","done":false},{"text":"Fuzz commands, corpus manifest, and passing evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:36Z","description":"Create a reproducible fuzz and property-test surface for untrusted packet and HEV-facing frame parsing so malformed lengths, families, and datagram sizes cannot trigger crashes, hangs, out-of-bounds access, or allocation growth.","id":"TASK-260715-52h8i3","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-packet-frame-fuzz-and-allocation-bounds-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: four-byte family headers; undersized and oversized datagrams; unknown families; random payloads; boundary MTUs; coalesced test inputs split into datagrams; corpus seeds from unit failures; deterministic property checks; allocation and runtime ceilings; crash minimization and replay. Out of scope: SSH and relay framing, kernel fuzzing, private API, performance acceptance, and treating a short fuzz run as exhaustive security proof.","status":"backlog","title":"Add packet-frame fuzz and allocation-bound tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped result matrix records device, OS, source and dependency revisions, exact config, duration, traffic generator, address family, MTU, requested and effective buffers, and raw artifact locations for every run. 2. All three MTUs run on both platforms under nominal and induced pressure; any unavailable IPv6 or NAT64 row is a named blocker or separately approved gap. 3. Nominal runs show no ordinary unexplained loss, while constrained and stalled runs show only bounded reason-specific drops and recover without task or descriptor growth. 4. Reports include latency, throughput, CPU, energy where available, packet and syscall rates, fragmentation observations, effective limits, and maximum datagram size. 5. The analysis recommends an MTU and buffer range from measured tradeoffs and does not accept 8500 solely because it is the upstream default.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-35wctc","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2jatnd"],"checklist":[{"text":"All MTU, platform, family, and pressure rows have reproducible run metadata","done":false},{"text":"Nominal correctness and induced bounded-drop expectations are satisfied","done":false},{"text":"Raw evidence and analyzed matrix are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:36Z","description":"Measure packet correctness and performance for MTUs 1500, 4096, and 8500 across physical iPhone and macOS environments under nominal, constrained-buffer, receiver-stall, and mixed traffic. Produce the evidence for an M0 MTU and socket-buffer baseline.","id":"TASK-260715-gyg51r","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-physical-mtu-and-socket-pressure-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: physical baseline iPhone and Apple-silicon Mac; IPv4, native IPv6 where available, dual stack, and recorded NAT64 substitute or gap; short web-like flows, large upload and download, DNS-sized packets, datagram bursts, and mixed bidirectional load; requested and effective socket buffers; packet, byte, batch, drop, latency, CPU, energy, syscall, fragmentation, and maximum-datagram metrics. Out of scope: SSH transport, remote relay correctness, production routing, unsupported performance extrapolation, and tuning outside fixed memory ceilings.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the physical MTU and socket-pressure matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped design states which component creates, owns, transfers, closes, and observes each descriptor and asynchronous task for start, cancellation, failure, and stop. 2. Forward and reverse framing algorithms define byte order, IPv4 and IPv6 classification, malformed-frame behavior, packet-boundary preservation, and batch construction. 3. EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, ENOBUFS, EMSGSIZE, EOF, cancellation, and persistent errors each have one explicit state transition, counter, and logging rule. 4. Batch count and elapsed-time budgets, queue nonexistence, metric units, counter monotonicity, and maximum-datagram tracking are testable. 5. The contract explicitly prohibits utun control access, file-descriptor scanning, reopening system descriptors, unbounded retries, and unbounded side buffers.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-uopycx"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3o0co4"],"checklist":[{"text":"Descriptor ownership and lifecycle are unambiguous","done":false},{"text":"Framing, bounded-work, error, metric, and test-seam contracts are exact","done":false},{"text":"The reviewed design is attached as a TASK-ID-scoped outcome resource","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:34Z","description":"Turn the packet-plane specification into an implementation-level bridge contract that fixes descriptor ownership, execution context, framing, socket configuration, bounded work, error semantics, counters, cancellation, and test seams before code is written.","id":"TASK-260715-p89bdj","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-packet-flow-bridge-contract","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM socket-pair lifecycle; endpoint ownership; nonblocking flags; SO_SNDBUF and SO_RCVBUF request and readback; Darwin family headers; batch and time budgets; bounded loss; EMSGSIZE and persistent-error startup failure; NEPacketTunnelFlow async boundaries; metric schema; privacy-safe errors; injectable socket and clock seams. Out of scope: choosing final measured buffer, MTU, or batch constants; HEV internals; SSH; routes; DNS; and private utun access.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the PacketFlowBridge concurrency and observability contract","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:28Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped dependency manifest records exact commits, submodule or vendored relationships, hashes, build flags, target architectures, upstream URLs, and inspected file paths. 2. Primary-source evidence confirms the packet descriptor contract, four-byte Darwin family header expectations, UDP-in-TCP framing, and every configured low-memory key. 3. MIT and bundled lwIP notice obligations are enumerated and sample binary-distribution notices are generated from the pinned sources. 4. Apple provider and harness build risks, global state, threading model, allocator hooks, shutdown contract, and known patches are documented. 5. The baseline declares unmodified upstream as default and defines the evidence required before any fork.","assignee":"","blockedBy":[],"blocks":["TASK-260715-p89bdj","TASK-260715-1vv52g"],"checklist":[{"text":"Exact HEV, core, task-system, and lwIP revisions and hashes are pinned","done":false},{"text":"Descriptor, framing, configuration, lifecycle, and license claims are source-backed","done":false},{"text":"The manifest and notice audit are attached as TASK-ID-scoped outcomes","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:34Z","description":"Establish the exact upstream HEV dependency set used by the M0 bridge spike and verify its Apple build, descriptor contract, UDP-in-TCP framing, configuration keys, licenses, notices, and fork baseline from primary source.","id":"TASK-260715-uopycx","isBlocked":false,"name":"pin-and-audit-hev-lwip-baseline","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: hev-socks5-tunnel, hev-socks5-core, hev-task-system, bundled lwIP, exact commits and submodules, source hashes, Apple build instructions, descriptor ownership, Darwin family header behavior, socks5.udp tcp mode, low-memory settings, licenses, notices, and upstream issue or patch inventory. Out of scope: modifying upstream, implementing the bridge, selecting production performance constants, or accepting an unpinned release tag.","status":"backlog","title":"Pin and audit the HEV and lwIP baseline","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:28Z"}]
.task-board/.resources/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:5736:[{"ac":"1. The adapter satisfies every compile-time conformance requirement and exposes no ReluxNIOSSH type across the shared transport boundary. 2. Host-key material reaches policy before authentication acceptance and first-use, match, rejection, and change smoke paths are observable. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec channels support bounded writes, reads, EOF, half-close, cancellation, and independent close with configurable receive windows. 4. Byte and time rekey thresholds, server requests, keepalive, connection and channel metrics, and privacy-safe errors are wired to the common schema. 5. The adapter builds and smoke-connects in macOS harness, macOS provider, iOS simulator, and Gate P0 iPhone configurations with pinned dependency evidence.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-nzdzv3","TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-1g9cyt","TASK-260715-pmww4f"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-3ikonq"],"checklist":[{"text":"Adapter fully conforms without leaking candidate types","done":false},{"text":"Host key, channels, windows, rekey, cancellation, and metrics are wired","done":false},{"text":"Apple-target and harness build or smoke evidence is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:15Z","description":"Implement the candidate adapter behind the common SSH transport contract and build it through the generated native and Swift dependency seams in the macOS harness and both Apple provider configurations.","id":"TASK-260715-1af33i","isBlocked":true,"name":"integrate-reluxniossh-candidate-adapter","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: pinned fork dependency; client bootstrap; raw host-key callback; approved public-key authentication; direct-tcpip; bidirectional exec; bounded async reads and writes; per-channel windows; automatic and explicit rekey; keepalive; cancellation; metrics; error mapping; harness registration; iOS and macOS compile and smoke paths. Out of scope: selecting NIOSSH, production lane scheduler, relay protocol, SFTP, password prompts, ProxyJump, agent forwarding, and candidate-specific types outside the adapter module.","status":"backlog","title":"Integrate the ReluxNIOSSH candidate adapter","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped ADR maps every required gate to row-level evidence for both candidates and marks pass, fail, or not run with reason. 2. The selected engine passes every mandatory gate, including Apple targets, pre-auth host evidence, approved auth, hundreds of direct channels, long-lived exec, configurable windows, client and server rekey, real relux compatibility, extension memory, and leak-free lifecycle. 3. A red preferred candidate routes selection to the alternate or returns the story to analysis; no threshold is weakened after results are known. 4. The ADR records exact dependency pins, adapter boundary, approved algorithms, initial window and rekey policy ranges, license notices, security monitoring, and fork or upstream-rebase owner. 5. Rejected evidence, residual risks, device and server revalidation triggers, and downstream tasks unblocked for M1 and M2 are explicit.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-1u2vpc","TASK-260715-2xx2tk"],"blocks":[],"checklist":[{"text":"Every mandatory gate maps to evidence for both candidates","done":false},{"text":"The selected engine has no waived red gate","done":false},{"text":"Pins, maintenance obligations, residual risks, and the selection ADR are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:17Z","description":"Select the production SSH engine only from audited build, conformance, functional, compatibility, rekey, scale, lifecycle, and memory evidence. Document the rejected candidate and maintenance obligations without weakening a failed gate.","id":"TASK-260715-1gjxer","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-m0-ssh-engine-selection","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: every M0 SSH gate; candidate versions; Apple integration; host verification; auth and algorithm support; direct-tcpip; exec; windows; rekey; backpressure; cancellation; compatibility; scale; memory; lifecycle; security and license posture; fork and upstream strategy; residual risks; revalidation triggers; downstream readiness. Out of scope: implementing lane scheduling, relay protocol, profile UX, SFTP, ProxyJump, release approval, and selecting a candidate with a waived mandatory gate.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the M0 SSH engine selection","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. The adapter builds from pinned source with the approved crypto backend for macOS harness, macOS provider, iOS simulator, and Gate P0 iPhone configurations and exposes no libssh2 type across the shared boundary. 2. Socket readiness and LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN are integrated without busy spinning or unbounded buffering, with deterministic cancellation and timeout behavior. 3. Raw host-key evidence, public-key auth, direct-tcpip, bidirectional exec, EOF and half-close, keepalive, metrics, and privacy-safe errors conform or are marked red with reproducible evidence. 4. Initial channel window and adjustment control plus client and server rekey behavior are proven through supported APIs or explicitly fail the candidate; no hidden fallback weakens the contract. 5. Repeated connect and cancel smoke runs return sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, and custom allocations to baseline.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k","TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-1g9cyt","TASK-260715-pmww4f"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-1u2vpc"],"checklist":[{"text":"Extension-safe libssh2 adapter and nonblocking integration build reproducibly","done":false},{"text":"Unsupported window or rekey behavior is recorded red rather than bypassed","done":false},{"text":"Harness and Apple-target conformance evidence is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:15Z","description":"Implement the libssh2 candidate behind the common SSH transport contract, including nonblocking socket integration and bounded async adaptation, and build it in the macOS harness and both Apple provider configurations without masking unsupported gates.","id":"TASK-260715-1ozsb6","isBlocked":true,"name":"integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: pinned libssh2 and crypto backend; extension-safe static or source build; session handshake; raw host-key access; approved public-key auth; direct-tcpip; bidirectional exec; custom receive-window experiment; rekey behavior; nonblocking EAGAIN integration; bounded buffers; cancellation; keepalive; metrics; error mapping; allocator hooks where supported; harness registration. Out of scope: patching libssh2 to force a pass without a separate recorded decision, blocking calls on provider executors, SFTP, password prompts, ProxyJump, agent forwarding, production lane scheduling, and candidate types outside the adapter.","status":"backlog","title":"Integrate the libssh2 candidate adapter","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records device, OS, server, source and dependency revisions, crypto backend, algorithms, config, windows, traffic, duration, loss and latency, counters, resources, raw artifact locations, and pass or fail for every row. 2. Raw host-key evidence precedes auth acceptance and Ed25519 plus the approved fallback pass against all in-scope servers, including real relux. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec remain correct under concurrent activity, nonblocking pressure, half-close, reset, cancellation, and provider lifecycle. 4. Window and rekey rows prove the required control through supported behavior or remain explicit red; a safe 5 GiB mixed run verifies content and resource cleanup when the candidate reaches that gate. 5. Any red row remains red, creates or references focused rework, and is not waived because another libssh2 feature passes.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-2ayxqn"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2xx2tk","TASK-260715-1gjxer"],"checklist":[{"text":"Every libssh2 functional, compatibility, Apple, and rekey row has metadata","done":false},{"text":"Window and rekey gaps remain explicit red with reproducible evidence","done":false},{"text":"Safe mixed-traffic and cleanup evidence plus the full matrix are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:16Z","description":"Execute the complete candidate-neutral functional, compatibility, Apple-target, and rekey matrix against the libssh2 adapter and preserve row-level evidence, including explicit red results for unsupported window or rekey control.","id":"TASK-260715-1u2vpc","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-libssh2-functional-and-rekey-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: macOS harness and provider; Gate P0 physical iPhone provider smoke; current OpenSSH Linux and macOS; older profile; real relux host; host verification; Ed25519 and fallback auth; direct-tcpip; exec stdio; 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped BDP window attempts; bounded pressure; client byte and time rekey attempts; server rekey; at least 5 GiB mixed traffic when safe; cancellation and network loss. Out of scope: NIOSSH results, production lane scheduling, SFTP, release distribution, patching the library inside the measurement task, and waiving an unavailable API.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the libssh2 functional and rekey matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped manifest records exact commits, tags where applicable, transitive dependencies, hashes, crypto backend, build flags, upstream URLs, licenses, notices, and inspected source paths. 2. A capability table maps every M0 SSH gate to a public API, internal hook, confirmed absence, or experiment still required for each candidate. 3. The SwiftNIO SSH 16 MiB child-window default and non-public client rekey surface are verified at the pinned source; libssh2 window and rekey behavior is equally source-pinned. 4. Current security advisories, maintenance cadence, extension constraints, threading, allocator, and binary-size risks are recorded. 5. Unknowns become concrete dependent experiments and no candidate is favored by weakening a missing capability.","assignee":"","blockedBy":[],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-nzdzv3","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-39xz9g"],"checklist":[{"text":"Both candidate and transitive revisions, hashes, licenses, and security baselines are pinned","done":false},{"text":"Every M0 gate maps to source evidence or a named experiment","done":false},{"text":"The candidate manifest and capability table are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:14Z","description":"Establish exact source baselines for SwiftNIO SSH and libssh2 and document their current Apple integration, host-key, authentication, channel, window, rekey, cancellation, algorithm, license, security, and maintenance surfaces before candidate work begins.","id":"TASK-260715-28ok1k","isBlocked":false,"name":"pin-and-audit-ssh-engine-candidates","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: the inspected SwiftNIO SSH commit and transitive SwiftNIO pins; a specific libssh2 commit or release and crypto backend; source hashes; licenses and notices; iOS and macOS build support; extension safety; known CVEs and advisories; raw host-key access; auth algorithms; direct-tcpip and exec; initial windows; rekey APIs; thread and allocator model; cancellation; open upstream issues. Out of scope: changing candidate code, selecting the winner, configuring production lanes, SFTP, or accepting marketing claims without source evidence.","status":"backlog","title":"Pin and audit the SSH engine candidates","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:30Z"},{"ac":"1. The same named suite runs against both adapters with candidate selection as data, and every gate has an explicit assertion rather than an informal log check. 2. Host verification tests prove policy sees raw key evidence before authentication acceptance and rejects a changed key without opening destination channels. 3. Channel tests verify independent open, bounded write, read, EOF, half-close, reset, cancel, close, and per-channel windows under concurrent activity. 4. Fake-clock and byte-count tests trigger client rekey; fixture-driven tests cover server rekey and active channels across key exchange. 5. Repeated cancellation at connection and channel states returns task, channel, socket, and descriptor counts to baseline and metrics use the common schema.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-39xz9g"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-1u2vpc"],"checklist":[{"text":"One candidate-neutral Swift Testing suite asserts every functional gate","done":false},{"text":"Host policy, windows, rekey, backpressure, and cancellation are deterministic","done":false},{"text":"Test inventory and passing or red candidate evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:16Z","description":"Implement one Swift Testing and harness suite that runs unchanged against both candidate adapters and verifies host policy, auth, channel semantics, exec, windows, rekey, backpressure, cancellation, metrics, and resource cleanup.","id":"TASK-260715-2d3g5e","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-common-ssh-transport-conformance-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: fake-clock and deterministic socket or server fixtures; host-key first use, match, change, and rejection; Ed25519 and fallback auth; direct-tcpip and exec; concurrent channels; bounded write pressure; EOF, half-close, reset, and early close; window profiles; client byte and time rekey; server rekey; keepalive; cancellation at each state; metrics and descriptor baselines. Out of scope: candidate-specific pass exceptions, production lane scheduling, full physical performance matrix, relay framing, UI, and tests that rely only on sleeps.","status":"backlog","title":"Add common SSH transport conformance tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped contract defines every operation, state transition, cancellation point, timeout, ownership boundary, error, metric, and privacy rule required by the M0 matrix. 2. Host-key bytes, algorithm, and fingerprint evidence are available to policy before authentication acceptance, including first-use, match, and change cases. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec channels have explicit open, bounded write, read, EOF, half-close, reset, cancel, and close semantics. 4. Window policy, WINDOW_ADJUST, automatic byte and time rekey, explicit test trigger, server rekey, keepalive, and key-exchange channel behavior are independently observable. 5. The conformance contract can be implemented by either candidate without exposing candidate types to ReluxTunnelCore consumers.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-nzdzv3","TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-2d3g5e"],"checklist":[{"text":"Candidate-neutral channel, lifecycle, error, and metric semantics are exact","done":false},{"text":"Host verification, windows, rekey, and bounded backpressure are independently testable","done":false},{"text":"The reviewed conformance contract is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:14Z","description":"Translate the SSH transport specification into a candidate-neutral implementation and test contract for connection, host verification, authentication, direct-tcpip, exec, windows, rekey, backpressure, cancellation, metrics, and lifecycle.","id":"TASK-260715-2ny6z4","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-ssh-transport-conformance-contract","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: Swift async interface and state ownership; raw host-key evidence before acceptance; supported auth outcomes; destination and originator endpoints; byte-channel and exec semantics; bounded write contract; half-close; per-channel receive windows and adjustment; client byte and time rekey; server rekey; keepalive; cancellation; error taxonomy; metric schema; lane identity for experiments; dependency injection. Out of scope: choosing a candidate, production lane scheduling, flow migration, SFTP, ProxyJump, interactive UI, relay framing, and final window constants.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the SSH transport conformance contract","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:30Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped comparative matrix records identical fixture, device, OS, source, dependency, algorithm, traffic, window, connection-count, loss, duration, and measurement inputs for both candidates. 2. Staged channel counts stop at each candidate safe ceiling with explicit reason; hundreds of independent channels must pass for a selectable candidate. 3. One, two, and four connection trials report throughput, latency, CPU, physical footprint and peak, available-memory samples, queued bytes, window credit, channels, tasks, sockets, descriptors, and failures. 4. At least one hundred connect, active-traffic, cancel, and close cycles show no monotonic resource growth for a selectable candidate. 5. The report estimates remaining extension budget after HEV and bridge baselines, distinguishes reserved window credit from measured allocation, and preserves all red lifecycle or memory rows.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-1u2vpc","TASK-260715-2jatnd"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-1gjxer"],"checklist":[{"text":"Both viable candidates use identical scale and impairment inputs","done":false},{"text":"Hundreds of channels, connection counts, memory, and lifecycle cleanup are evidenced","done":false},{"text":"Comparative raw data and budget analysis are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:17Z","description":"Measure both viable candidates under identical concurrent-channel, connection-count, loss, cancellation, and memory conditions so engine selection accounts for extension budgets and cross-flow behavior rather than functional support alone.","id":"TASK-260715-2xx2tk","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-comparative-ssh-scale-memory-and-lifecycle-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: staged 100, 250, 500, and measured safe channel counts; control-like, ordinary, bulk, early-close, half-close, and idle mixes; one, two, and four independent SSH connections; 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped BDP windows; Wi-Fi-like latency and loss; connection and control-lane failure simulation; repeated connect and close; physical iPhone and Mac footprint; CPU; queued bytes; descriptors; tasks; custom allocator metrics where available. Out of scope: production lane scheduler, flow migration, QUIC policy, forcing a functionally red candidate through unsafe scale tests, and claiming advertised windows are eagerly allocated.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the comparative SSH scale, memory, and lifecycle matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped fixture manifest records server OS and OpenSSH versions, configurations, algorithms, host-key fingerprints, user-key types, destination services, traffic seeds, network profiles, and reproduction or teardown steps. 2. Current Linux, current macOS, one approved older compatibility profile, and the real relux host are reachable through least-privilege test identities. 3. Fixtures deterministically produce success, host-key first use, host-key change, auth rejection, channel rejection, early close, half-close, reset, server rekey, latency, loss, and disconnect conditions. 4. A 5 GiB or larger reproducible source and sink verifies byte counts and content hashes without retaining payload. 5. Secrets remain in an approved external store; artifacts contain only public keys, fingerprints, non-secret configuration, and secret-reference names.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2d3g5e"],"checklist":[{"text":"Server, key, algorithm, traffic, and impairment fixtures cover every matrix branch","done":false},{"text":"The real relux host is represented with least-privilege test access","done":false},{"text":"Privacy-safe fixture manifest and teardown evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:15Z","description":"Create the controlled server, key, algorithm, traffic, and network-condition fixtures required to run identical M0 matrices against both candidates, including the real relux server without exposing production credentials.","id":"TASK-260715-39xz9g","isBlocked":true,"name":"provision-reproducible-ssh-matrix-fixtures","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: current OpenSSH Linux and macOS endpoints; documented approved older algorithm profile; Ed25519 host and user keys; approved fallback host and user key types; host-key change fixture; direct-tcpip destinations; long-lived stdio exec echo or sink; at least 5 GiB deterministic traffic; latency and loss controls; early close and reset endpoints; real relux test host access; credential rotation and cleanup. Out of scope: production user data, broad Internet exposure, password or interactive auth, persistent root service, relay implementation, and storing private test credentials in git or board resources.","status":"backlog","title":"Provision reproducible SSH matrix fixtures","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records device, OS, server, source and dependency revisions, algorithms, config, windows, traffic, duration, loss and latency, counters, resources, raw artifact locations, and pass or fail for every required row. 2. Raw host-key evidence precedes auth acceptance and Ed25519 plus the approved fallback pass against all in-scope servers, including real relux. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec remain correct under concurrent activity, pressure, half-close, reset, cancellation, and provider lifecycle. 4. Client byte and time rekeys plus server rekey survive at least 5 GiB of simultaneous direct and exec traffic without corruption, deadlock, or channel leak. 5. Any red row remains red, creates or references focused rework, and is not waived by the candidate implementation team.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-2ayxqn"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2xx2tk","TASK-260715-1gjxer"],"checklist":[{"text":"Every ReluxNIOSSH functional, compatibility, Apple, and rekey row has metadata","done":false},{"text":"The 5 GiB mixed rekey run verifies hashes and resource cleanup","done":false},{"text":"Red rows are preserved and the full evidence matrix is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:16Z","description":"Execute the complete candidate-neutral functional, compatibility, Apple-target, and rekey matrix against the ReluxNIOSSH adapter and preserve row-level evidence without treating the existence of the fork as a reason to accept it.","id":"TASK-260715-3ikonq","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-reluxniossh-functional-and-rekey-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: macOS harness and provider; Gate P0 physical iPhone provider smoke; current OpenSSH Linux and macOS; older profile; real relux host; host verification; Ed25519 and fallback auth; direct-tcpip; exec stdio; 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped BDP windows; bounded pressure; client byte and time rekey; server rekey; at least 5 GiB mixed traffic; cancellation and network loss. Out of scope: libssh2 results, production lane scheduling, SFTP, release distribution, and fixing failures inside the measurement task.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the ReluxNIOSSH functional and rekey matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. The fork is based on the exact audited commit and each patch maps only to configurable channel windows, automatic client rekey, or tests and documentation for those behaviors. 2. Tests cover 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and larger capped windows, adjustment suppression, byte threshold, time threshold with injected clock, simultaneous threshold requests, active channels during rekey, and server-initiated rekey. 3. Default upstream behavior remains source-compatible unless the adapter opts into Relux policy. 4. A patch manifest, license review, upstream comparison, rebase procedure, conflict test command, and candidate upstreaming plan are attached. 5. No internal test-only symbol is called through reflection or other fragile access from product code.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k","TASK-260715-2ny6z4"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-1af33i"],"checklist":[{"text":"Fork patches are minimal and trace only to window and rekey requirements","done":false},{"text":"Deterministic upstream-style tests cover all new policy behavior","done":false},{"text":"Patch manifest, upstream diff, and rebase plan are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:14Z","description":"Create the smallest upstream-trackable SwiftNIO SSH patch set that makes child-channel receive-window policy configurable and exposes safe automatic client byte and time rekey while preserving server-initiated rekey behavior.","id":"TASK-260715-nzdzv3","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-minimal-reluxniossh-fork","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: fork from the pinned commit; configurable initial child windows and adjustment hooks; automatic byte and elapsed-time thresholds; safe request coalescing and key-exchange state; public or package API needed by the adapter; focused upstream-style tests; commit and patch inventory; notices; upstream tracking and rebase instructions. Out of scope: unrelated refactors, new SSH features, production lane scheduling, changing cryptographic algorithms, hiding failing tests, or retaining patches not required by the two blocked gates.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement the minimal ReluxNIOSSH fork","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:30Z"}]
.task-board/.resources/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:9826:[{"ac":"1. A dated evidence dossier cites the controlling Apple sources and describes the complete packet, TCP, SSH, DNS, and exit-host behavior without euphemism. 2. The dossier identifies the TN3120 ambiguity and asks a decision-capable Apple channel a concrete intended-use and distribution question. 3. Gate evidence is one of the accepted forms: written DTS response, entitlement or review feedback for an accurately disclosed prototype, or an approved architecture change that carries packet semantics to a remote VPN endpoint. 4. Reproducible artifacts record submission text, dates, case or review identifiers, responses, redactions, and source revision. 5. A decision record declares pass, fail, or pivot, states constraints and affected downstream work, and leaves production tasks blocked on any negative or ambiguous result.","assignee":"","blockedBy":[],"blocks":["STORY-260715-l2i2oo"],"checklist":[],"children":["TASK-260715-12avq0","TASK-260715-1828xy","TASK-260715-1i6bh7","TASK-260715-1o3q6l","TASK-260715-x4h9n1"],"created":"2026-07-15T00:46:59Z","description":"Establish authoritative, reviewable evidence that the disclosed Relux data plane qualifies for the intended Network Extension packet-tunnel entitlement and App Store distribution, or record an architecture pivot before any production implementation is accepted. The disclosure must state that HEV terminates device TCP locally and that user payload then travels only inside authenticated SSH connections to a user-selected remote exit host.","id":"STORY-260715-2itwz7","isBlocked":false,"name":"apple-platform-intent-gate","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: point-in-time primary Apple guidance; an exact architecture and data-flow disclosure; selection and execution of an accepted evidence route through Apple Developer Technical Support, entitlement feedback, accurately disclosed prototype review, or a packet-semantic remote-endpoint pivot; preservation of submissions, responses, constraints, and a Gate A0 decision. Out of scope: production tunnel code, claims of approval inferred only from local installation, marketing language, and regional legal analysis beyond recording a required follow-up.","status":"to-dev","title":"Gate A0 — Apple packet-tunnel intended-use viability","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:21Z"},{"ac":"1. Evidence confirms Relux Works organization enrollment, team identifier, responsible roles, registered physical devices, and access to manage identifiers, capabilities, certificates, and profiles. 2. A reviewed identity matrix defines unique iOS and macOS host and extension bundle IDs plus the minimum App Group and Keychain groups. 3. Host and extension App IDs and development profiles contain the exact required packet-tunnel, App Group, and Keychain entitlements with no unrelated capability. 4. A disposable provider is installed through its containing app, saves a NETunnelProviderManager configuration, launches, reports a versioned probe result, and stops cleanly on one named physical iPhone and one named Apple-silicon Mac. 5. Exported entitlement and profile inspections match the planned matrix and contain no secret material. 6. A Gate P0 record includes device and OS versions, Xcode and source revisions, bundle/profile identifiers, commands or steps, observed results, failures, and an explicit pass or fail verdict.","assignee":"","blockedBy":[],"blocks":["STORY-260715-l2i2oo","STORY-260715-lkshfz"],"checklist":[],"children":["TASK-260715-1jckn0","TASK-260715-1kntdx","TASK-260715-1r0fxv","TASK-260715-2ayxqn","TASK-260715-3jloqy","TASK-260715-9yp8to","TASK-260715-apc34w","TASK-260715-ypo7yo"],"created":"2026-07-15T00:46:59Z","description":"Prove that the Relux Works organization can provision the required host and packet-tunnel extension identities and can install and launch a minimally functional custom VPN provider on a physical iPhone and an Apple-silicon Mac. The result is a reproducible signing and entitlement baseline for later M0 integration, not a production VPN.","id":"STORY-260715-2xnj3v","isBlocked":false,"name":"apple-capability-provisioning","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: organization enrollment and required roles; bundle ID, App Group, and Keychain access-group naming; Network Extension packet-tunnel capabilities; development certificates and profiles; disposable iOS and macOS host/provider probes; NETunnelProviderManager configuration; entitlement and embedded-profile inspection; physical-device install, launch, start, and stop evidence. Out of scope: TestFlight or App Store release, Developer ID notarization, production UI, packet forwarding, SSH transport, relay behavior, and storage of certificates, private keys, credentials, or provisioning secrets in the repository or board.","status":"to-dev","title":"Gate P0 — Apple capabilities and physical-device provisioning","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"},{"ac":"1. The spike uses only NEPacketTunnelFlow and documented Darwin socket APIs and contains no utun control access, descriptor discovery, or private API. 2. Forward and reverse paths preserve packet boundaries, add or validate and strip network-byte-order AF_INET or AF_INET6 headers, batch writes, and count malformed or unsupported frames. 3. EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, and ENOBUFS cause bounded reason-specific drops; EMSGSIZE fails start with attempted and effective limits; persistent errors and cancellation release all tasks and descriptors. 4. Upstream HEV runs with socks5.udp set to tcp and the stated low-memory baseline, and its internal SOCKS endpoint rejects unowned ingress. 5. Swift Testing and fault-injection coverage verifies framing, batching budgets, saturation, MTU errors, cleanup, repeated start and stop, IPv4, and IPv6. 6. Physical iPhone and macOS evidence covers MTUs 1500, 4096, and 8500; constrained buffers; receiver stalls; nominal mixed traffic; staged concurrency; and lifecycle loops with device, OS, revisions, traffic shape, counters, descriptors, CPU, syscall rate, physical footprint, peak, and available-memory samples. 7. A gate report selects measured MTU, buffer, batch, and session baselines, states whether the 25–30 MiB target is met, and permits a HEV fork only when Instruments evidence shows a material bottleneck and a measured callback improvement.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["STORY-260715-l2i2oo"],"blocks":["STORY-260715-lkshfz"],"checklist":[],"children":["TASK-260715-135rr8","TASK-260715-1vv52g","TASK-260715-2jatnd","TASK-260715-35wctc","TASK-260715-3dn813","TASK-260715-3o0co4","TASK-260715-52h8i3","TASK-260715-gyg51r","TASK-260715-p89bdj","TASK-260715-uopycx"],"created":"2026-07-15T00:46:59Z","description":"Prove on macOS and a physical iPhone that public Network Extension packetFlow APIs can exchange bounded datagrams with unmodified upstream HEV and bundled lwIP through a nonblocking AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM socket pair, with correct Darwin family framing, backpressure, cleanup, instrumentation, MTU behavior, and an extension memory baseline.","id":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","isBlocked":true,"name":"packet-bridge-hev-spike","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: pinned upstream HEV, core, task-system, and lwIP revisions and notices; Swift PacketFlowBridge; Darwin four-byte family headers; nonblocking socket buffers and effective-limit inspection; bounded batching and time budgets; reason-specific drops and fatal-error semantics; fixed HEV UDP-in-TCP mode; process-local SOCKS boundary; IPv4 and IPv6 traffic; MTU 1500, 4096, and 8500; socket pressure; repeated lifecycle and concurrency tests; physical footprint and available-memory evidence; fork-versus-upstream decision. Out of scope: private utun discovery, file-descriptor scanning, SSH transport, remote UDP relay, production route or DNS policy, lane scheduling, full application UX, and performance claims not backed by before-and-after measurements.","status":"to-dev","title":"M0 packetFlow, socket-pair, and HEV bridge spike","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"},{"ac":"1. An architecture decision records the chosen generator, exact supported deployment targets, target graph, module ownership, dependency direction, configuration strategy, and reasons against viable alternatives. 2. Clean generation produces buildable ReluxProxyMac, ReluxProxyMacTunnel, ReluxProxyIOS, ReluxProxyIOSTunnel, ReluxTunnelCore, ReluxTunnelHarness, relux-relay, and protocol-test targets with deterministic identifiers and schemes. 3. Both providers are thin adapters that depend on shared core contracts and do not duplicate packet, SSH, relay, lifecycle, or memory state machines. 4. Native Swift and C dependencies can be pinned, licensed, and linked without dynamic-library or App Store extension violations. 5. Credential-free CI or local verification builds every target and runs shared tests; signed physical-device configurations consume Gate P0 identities without committing secrets. 6. The existing SwiftPM tests, manual SOCKS app build, defaults, and release path remain reproducible until an explicit migration decision says otherwise. 7. Developer documentation explains generation, target ownership, signing inputs, artifact locations, and how to run the harness.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["STORY-260715-2itwz7","STORY-260715-2xnj3v"],"blocks":["STORY-260715-jnpbyz","STORY-260715-lkshfz"],"checklist":[],"children":["TASK-260715-14lk3y","TASK-260715-1ccx3l","TASK-260715-1fv4z1","TASK-260715-1g9cyt","TASK-260715-2btjwm","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-32umrc","TASK-260715-33oofa","TASK-260715-3bdplx","TASK-260715-3r0993","TASK-260715-d6x51z","TASK-260715-nphtib","TASK-260715-pmww4f","TASK-260715-sbrrp7","TASK-260715-uyju7n"],"created":"2026-07-15T00:46:59Z","description":"Replace the single-target SwiftPM-only project shape with a reproducibly generated Apple workspace foundation that can embed iOS and macOS packet-tunnel extensions while preserving the currently shipped macOS SOCKS application until a separate migration decision retires or replaces it. Establish thin platform adapters, a shared ReluxTunnelCore boundary, native dependency seams, a fast macOS harness, and relay target placeholders without implementing production tunnel behavior.","id":"STORY-260715-l2i2oo","isBlocked":true,"name":"target-project-architecture","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: current-state and migration inventory; Tuist-versus-alternative and deployment-target evidence; target and configuration graph; iOS and macOS host and packet-tunnel targets; ReluxTunnelCore Swift package; ReluxTunnelHarness CLI; portable relux-relay and protocol-test target shells; signing configuration seams; pinned native dependency integration strategy; clean generation, build, and test verification; legacy SwiftPM and release-path preservation; developer documentation. Out of scope: production packet forwarding, SSH engine selection, UDP relay protocol implementation, profile UX migration, full release automation, App Store submission, and retirement of the existing system-SSH app.","status":"to-dev","title":"Generated Apple multi-target project foundation","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"},{"ac":"1. Both candidates build in the macOS and iOS packet-tunnel target configurations, with pinned revisions, licenses, integration constraints, and reproducible build commands recorded. 2. One common conformance harness obtains raw host-key evidence before acceptance and exercises Ed25519 plus an approved fallback against current OpenSSH, documented older profiles, and the real relux host. 3. Candidate evidence covers independent direct-tcpip and bidirectional long-lived exec channels, early close and half-close, bounded backpressure, cancellation, network loss, reconnect, and no task, channel, socket, or descriptor growth across repeated cycles. 4. Initial receive windows and WINDOW_ADJUST behavior are configurable per channel; tests cover 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped bandwidth-delay-product profiles without multiplying a large default by maximum sessions. 5. Client byte and time thresholds and server requests survive at least 5 GiB of simultaneous direct-tcpip and exec traffic, with lane-local failure evidence. 6. Hundreds of concurrent channels and one, two, and four connection trials remain within the extension memory budget and record device, OS, revisions, algorithms, traffic, loss and latency, windows, queued bytes, CPU, physical footprint, peak, and failures. 7. A decision record selects only a candidate that passes every required gate, documents rejected results and residual risks, and routes a red primary candidate to the alternate rather than weakening criteria.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["STORY-260715-l2i2oo","STORY-260715-2xnj3v","STORY-260715-jnpbyz"],"blocks":[],"checklist":[],"children":["TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-1gjxer","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-1u2vpc","TASK-260715-28ok1k","TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-2xx2tk","TASK-260715-39xz9g","TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-nzdzv3"],"created":"2026-07-15T00:46:59Z","description":"Compare a minimal, upstream-trackable ReluxNIOSSH fork with libssh2 behind one spike transport contract and select an in-process engine only after one candidate passes the complete Apple-target, host-verification, authentication, direct-tcpip, exec, window, rekey, compatibility, backpressure, cancellation, lifecycle, and memory matrix.","id":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","isBlocked":true,"name":"ssh-engine-spike","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: pinned candidate revisions and licenses; iOS and macOS packet-tunnel-compatible static or source integration; raw host-key evidence; Ed25519 and approved fallback authentication; direct-tcpip and bidirectional exec channels; bounded writes; per-channel initial windows and adjustment policy; client byte and time rekey plus server rekey; keepalive, cancellation, metrics, and error mapping; current and supported older OpenSSH profiles plus the real relux server; hundreds of channels; at least 5 GiB mixed traffic; one, two, and four raw SSH connections; loss, reconnect, and descriptor tests; memory comparison; engine ADR and fork maintenance plan. Out of scope: SFTP, interactive shells, agent or X11 forwarding, password prompts, ProxyJump, production lane scheduling or flow migration, QUIC policy implementation, remote relay implementation, and weakening a failed gate to preserve a preferred candidate.","status":"to-dev","title":"M0 in-process SSH engine comparison and selection","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"}]
.task-board/.resources/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:9841:[{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records device and OS, source and dependency revisions, config, traffic, duration, flow counts, physical footprint, peak, available-memory samples, sessions, buffers, queued bytes, descriptors, tasks, drops, and failures. 2. Staged counts stop at the measured safe ceiling with an explicit reason; the task does not force 1200 sessions when the device budget rejects it. 3. At least one hundred start and stop cycles plus cancellation at multiple startup points show no monotonic descriptor, task, session, or physical-footprint growth. 4. Soft, pressure, and critical simulations verify the spike can reduce or stop work in the specified order or explicitly identify behavior deferred until SSH integration. 5. The report states whether the 25–30 MiB steady-state target is met, the remaining budget for SSH, DNS, relay, caches, and reconnect overlap, and every unresolved risk.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-35wctc","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2jatnd"],"checklist":[{"text":"Staged concurrency and lifecycle rows stop at measured safe limits","done":false},{"text":"Physical footprint, available memory, sessions, descriptors, tasks, and drops are recorded","done":false},{"text":"Budget analysis and reproducible raw evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:37Z","description":"Measure the full bridge and HEV baseline under staged flow counts, repeated provider lifecycle, cancellation, and pressure on the physical iPhone and Mac. Establish whether the provisional 25–30 MiB extension target and bounded resource contract are credible.","id":"TASK-260715-135rr8","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-physical-memory-lifecycle-and-concurrency-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: staged 100, 250, 500, and measured configuration-limit flows; many idle connections; mixed bidirectional traffic; start and stop loops; cancellation during start; host termination; sleep and wake where supported by the spike; induced memory pressure; physical footprint and peak; os_proc_available_memory samples; HEV sessions; socket buffers; queued bytes; descriptors; tasks; counters; reconnect-overlap estimate. Out of scope: claiming an Apple memory guarantee, SSH channel allocations not yet implemented, production reconnect, jetsam experimentation that risks device stability, and raising limits to hit an arbitrary count.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the physical memory, lifecycle, and concurrency matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. The exact pinned HEV sources build and link through the approved native packaging seam for macOS harness, macOS provider, iOS simulator, and iOS device configurations. 2. HEV receives only the bridge-owned endpoint and starts with the recorded MTU and exact UDP-in-TCP and low-memory configuration values. 3. The internal SOCKS endpoint is process-local or otherwise cryptographically or structurally restricted to the owned adapter path and rejects an external ingress test. 4. Startup failure and cancellation close HEV tasks, the transferred descriptor, listener state, and bridge resources without double close. 5. Required HEV, core, task-system, and lwIP notices are present in produced test bundles and trace to the pinned manifest.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-uopycx","TASK-260715-3o0co4","TASK-260715-1g9cyt"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-35wctc","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"checklist":[{"text":"Pinned unmodified HEV builds in harness and all Apple target configurations","done":false},{"text":"Fixed configuration and owned SOCKS boundary are enforced","done":false},{"text":"Lifecycle, linkage, and notice evidence is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:35Z","description":"Build the pinned unmodified HEV stack for the harness and both Apple provider configurations, hand it the owned socket-pair endpoint, apply the fixed UDP-in-TCP and low-memory baseline, and expose its process-local SOCKS side to an injectable adapter seam.","id":"TASK-260715-1vv52g","isBlocked":true,"name":"integrate-unmodified-hev-lwip-with-bridge","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: reproducible HEV builds; descriptor handoff; config generation; MTU input; socks5.udp tcp; task-stack-size 24576; tcp-buffer-size 4096; max-session-count 1200 baseline; process-local SOCKS listener or owned channel; startup health; coordinated shutdown; metrics and notice bundling. Out of scope: SSHProxyAdapter implementation, final memory constants, remote relay, fork patches, production routes and DNS, and acceptance of external SOCKS clients.","status":"backlog","title":"Integrate unmodified HEV and lwIP with the bridge","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped ADR links every required M0 Bridge row to reproducible evidence and marks pass, fail, or blocked without averaging away a red platform or address-family result. 2. The record selects initial MTU, requested socket buffers, batch count and time budgets, HEV settings, and measured session ceiling with rationale. 3. Pass requires public API only, correct IPv4 and IPv6 framing, bounded backpressure, clean lifecycle, no nominal unexplained loss, and physical-device memory headroom. 4. A fork is rejected by default and allowed only when Instruments identifies bridge copies or syscalls as a material bottleneck and a measured callback prototype improves it with regression coverage and rebase plan. 5. Residual risks, device and OS revalidation triggers, notices, and tasks unblocked for M1 are explicit.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-gyg51r","TASK-260715-135rr8"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2xx2tk"],"checklist":[{"text":"Every M0 Bridge gate row traces to reproducible evidence","done":false},{"text":"Configuration and memory baselines are selected without weakening red rows","done":false},{"text":"The fork disposition and TASK-ID-scoped ADR are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:37Z","description":"Consolidate implementation, deterministic tests, fuzzing, physical MTU, pressure, lifecycle, and memory evidence into the M0 Bridge gate decision, including initial configuration and the measured fork-versus-upstream disposition.","id":"TASK-260715-2jatnd","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-m0-packet-bridge-decision","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: public-API compliance; correctness; selected MTU, socket buffers, batch budgets, and session baseline; error and drop behavior; physical-device memory headroom; known gaps; upstream pin; notice status; fork decision; revalidation triggers; downstream M1 readiness. Out of scope: SSH or relay gate claims, production route and DNS approval, future performance guarantees, and authorizing a fork without Instruments evidence.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the M0 packet-bridge and HEV decision","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. Deterministic integration tests complete IPv4 and IPv6 TCP handshake, bidirectional stream, half-close, reset, and independent concurrent-flow scenarios through the real HEV binary. 2. The adapter fixture observes the expected SOCKS CONNECT and UDP-in-TCP contract, and an unowned client cannot use the internal endpoint. 3. Receiver stalls cause only bounded socket drops and recorded counters; no unbounded application queue appears. 4. Configuration tests prove the requested MTU and fixed low-memory and UDP settings reach HEV. 5. At least one hundred harness start, traffic, and stop cycles return tasks, descriptors, sessions, and allocated test resources to baseline.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3dn813","TASK-260715-1vv52g"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-gyg51r","TASK-260715-135rr8"],"checklist":[{"text":"Real HEV integration covers IPv4, IPv6, stream lifecycle, and SOCKS framing","done":false},{"text":"Stall and repeated lifecycle behavior remains bounded","done":false},{"text":"Integration test matrix and passing evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:36Z","description":"Exercise the real unmodified HEV stack through PacketFlowBridge in the macOS harness and Apple-provider test seams, proving IPv4 and IPv6 TCP translation, SOCKS contract behavior, configuration, backpressure propagation, and clean lifecycle before physical performance runs.","id":"TASK-260715-35wctc","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-hev-bridge-integration-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: real HEV and lwIP; synthetic packet endpoints; local SOCKS adapter fixture; IPv4 and IPv6 TCP handshakes and streams; half-close and reset; mixed small and bulk flows; UDP-in-TCP request framing exposure; internal endpoint rejection; induced stalls; startup and stop loops; observable counters. Out of scope: real SSH, remote UDP relay, default routes, system DNS, production internet destinations, and final throughput claims.","status":"backlog","title":"Add HEV bridge integration tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. Swift Testing cases cover forward and reverse IPv4 and IPv6 framing byte-for-byte and prove malformed or unknown frames are dropped with the correct counter. 2. Deterministic fault injection proves each bounded-drop errno, fatal EMSGSIZE metadata, persistent-error transition, and no retry or side-buffer behavior. 3. Batch-count and fake-clock time budgets stop work predictably and yield to other tasks. 4. Cancellation at every startup stage and at least one hundred start and stop cycles leave descriptor, task, and continuation counts at baseline. 5. Tests assert metric names, units, monotonic counters, effective buffer values, and maximum observed datagram size.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3o0co4"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-35wctc"],"checklist":[{"text":"Swift Testing covers every framing and errno branch deterministically","done":false},{"text":"Cancellation and repeated lifecycle return all tracked resources to baseline","done":false},{"text":"Test inventory and passing evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:35Z","description":"Create deterministic Swift Testing coverage for packet framing, batching, socket limits, backpressure, errors, cancellation, and resource cleanup using injected packet-flow, socket, clock, and fault controls.","id":"TASK-260715-3dn813","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-packet-flow-bridge-unit-and-fault-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: IPv4 and IPv6 family headers; endianness; empty, undersized, unknown-family, and oversized frames; packet boundaries; batch count and time budgets; effective-buffer readback; induced EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, ENOBUFS, EMSGSIZE, persistent errors, cancellation races, partial startup, repeated lifecycle, and descriptor accounting. Out of scope: HEV behavior, physical-device throughput, SSH, route or DNS integration, and tests that depend on arbitrary sleeps.","status":"backlog","title":"Add PacketFlowBridge unit and fault-injection tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. Static inspection and tests show that the implementation references only NEPacketTunnelFlow and documented Darwin socket APIs and never discovers or reopens utun descriptors. 2. Each packet read from packetFlow is sent as one datagram with the correct family header, and each valid reverse datagram becomes one packet with the matching protocol family. 3. Socket buffer requests and effective readbacks are exposed in metrics; EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, and ENOBUFS increment distinct drop counters without retry or side storage. 4. EMSGSIZE fails the current start with attempted datagram size and effective limit; persistent failures produce bounded privacy-safe errors. 5. All descriptors, read sources, continuations, and tasks close exactly once under normal stop, start failure, and cancellation.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-p89bdj","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-pmww4f"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3dn813","TASK-260715-1vv52g","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"checklist":[{"text":"Bridge implementation follows the approved public-API and ownership contract","done":false},{"text":"Backpressure, EMSGSIZE, metrics, and bounded batching are implemented","done":false},{"text":"Implementation notes and verification commands are attached as a TASK-ID-scoped outcome","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:35Z","description":"Implement the Swift bridge that exchanges packet batches between NEPacketTunnelFlow and the HEV descriptor endpoint through a nonblocking AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM socket pair, following the approved contract exactly.","id":"TASK-260715-3o0co4","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-public-socket-pair-packet-flow-bridge","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: socket-pair creation; close-on-exec and nonblocking configuration; socket-buffer request and effective-value readback; endpoint transfer; four-byte network-order AF_INET and AF_INET6 headers; batch reads and writes; count and time budgets; reason-specific counters; cancellation; privacy-safe failures; dependency injection. Out of scope: HEV startup, SSH, routes, DNS, private APIs, retries after bounded-queue drops, unbounded buffering, final tuning constants, and product UI.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement the public socket-pair PacketFlowBridge","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. The fuzz target or deterministic Swift property harness accepts arbitrary bytes and never reads beyond frame boundaries or allocates relative to an untrusted declared length beyond the configured datagram ceiling. 2. Seed corpus covers IPv4, IPv6, empty, 1–3 byte, unknown-family, exact MTU, over-MTU, and prior regression cases. 3. CI runs a bounded deterministic corpus; a documented extended command records seed, duration, iterations, peak allocation, and source revision. 4. Any crash or invariant violation produces a minimized replay fixture and concrete bug before this task can pass. 5. Passing evidence demonstrates bounded runtime and memory for the configured corpus and asserts reason-specific malformed counters.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3o0co4","TASK-260715-1vv52g"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-gyg51r","TASK-260715-135rr8"],"checklist":[{"text":"Arbitrary frame input is bounded by explicit length, allocation, and runtime ceilings","done":false},{"text":"Seed and regression corpus is replayable in CI","done":false},{"text":"Fuzz commands, corpus manifest, and passing evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:36Z","description":"Create a reproducible fuzz and property-test surface for untrusted packet and HEV-facing frame parsing so malformed lengths, families, and datagram sizes cannot trigger crashes, hangs, out-of-bounds access, or allocation growth.","id":"TASK-260715-52h8i3","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-packet-frame-fuzz-and-allocation-bounds-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: four-byte family headers; undersized and oversized datagrams; unknown families; random payloads; boundary MTUs; coalesced test inputs split into datagrams; corpus seeds from unit failures; deterministic property checks; allocation and runtime ceilings; crash minimization and replay. Out of scope: SSH and relay framing, kernel fuzzing, private API, performance acceptance, and treating a short fuzz run as exhaustive security proof.","status":"backlog","title":"Add packet-frame fuzz and allocation-bound tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped result matrix records device, OS, source and dependency revisions, exact config, duration, traffic generator, address family, MTU, requested and effective buffers, and raw artifact locations for every run. 2. All three MTUs run on both platforms under nominal and induced pressure; any unavailable IPv6 or NAT64 row is a named blocker or separately approved gap. 3. Nominal runs show no ordinary unexplained loss, while constrained and stalled runs show only bounded reason-specific drops and recover without task or descriptor growth. 4. Reports include latency, throughput, CPU, energy where available, packet and syscall rates, fragmentation observations, effective limits, and maximum datagram size. 5. The analysis recommends an MTU and buffer range from measured tradeoffs and does not accept 8500 solely because it is the upstream default.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-35wctc","TASK-260715-52h8i3"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2jatnd"],"checklist":[{"text":"All MTU, platform, family, and pressure rows have reproducible run metadata","done":false},{"text":"Nominal correctness and induced bounded-drop expectations are satisfied","done":false},{"text":"Raw evidence and analyzed matrix are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:36Z","description":"Measure packet correctness and performance for MTUs 1500, 4096, and 8500 across physical iPhone and macOS environments under nominal, constrained-buffer, receiver-stall, and mixed traffic. Produce the evidence for an M0 MTU and socket-buffer baseline.","id":"TASK-260715-gyg51r","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-physical-mtu-and-socket-pressure-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: physical baseline iPhone and Apple-silicon Mac; IPv4, native IPv6 where available, dual stack, and recorded NAT64 substitute or gap; short web-like flows, large upload and download, DNS-sized packets, datagram bursts, and mixed bidirectional load; requested and effective socket buffers; packet, byte, batch, drop, latency, CPU, energy, syscall, fragmentation, and maximum-datagram metrics. Out of scope: SSH transport, remote relay correctness, production routing, unsupported performance extrapolation, and tuning outside fixed memory ceilings.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the physical MTU and socket-pressure matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:29Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped design states which component creates, owns, transfers, closes, and observes each descriptor and asynchronous task for start, cancellation, failure, and stop. 2. Forward and reverse framing algorithms define byte order, IPv4 and IPv6 classification, malformed-frame behavior, packet-boundary preservation, and batch construction. 3. EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, ENOBUFS, EMSGSIZE, EOF, cancellation, and persistent errors each have one explicit state transition, counter, and logging rule. 4. Batch count and elapsed-time budgets, queue nonexistence, metric units, counter monotonicity, and maximum-datagram tracking are testable. 5. The contract explicitly prohibits utun control access, file-descriptor scanning, reopening system descriptors, unbounded retries, and unbounded side buffers.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-uopycx"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3o0co4"],"checklist":[{"text":"Descriptor ownership and lifecycle are unambiguous","done":false},{"text":"Framing, bounded-work, error, metric, and test-seam contracts are exact","done":false},{"text":"The reviewed design is attached as a TASK-ID-scoped outcome resource","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:34Z","description":"Turn the packet-plane specification into an implementation-level bridge contract that fixes descriptor ownership, execution context, framing, socket configuration, bounded work, error semantics, counters, cancellation, and test seams before code is written.","id":"TASK-260715-p89bdj","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-packet-flow-bridge-contract","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM socket-pair lifecycle; endpoint ownership; nonblocking flags; SO_SNDBUF and SO_RCVBUF request and readback; Darwin family headers; batch and time budgets; bounded loss; EMSGSIZE and persistent-error startup failure; NEPacketTunnelFlow async boundaries; metric schema; privacy-safe errors; injectable socket and clock seams. Out of scope: choosing final measured buffer, MTU, or batch constants; HEV internals; SSH; routes; DNS; and private utun access.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the PacketFlowBridge concurrency and observability contract","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:28Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped dependency manifest records exact commits, submodule or vendored relationships, hashes, build flags, target architectures, upstream URLs, and inspected file paths. 2. Primary-source evidence confirms the packet descriptor contract, four-byte Darwin family header expectations, UDP-in-TCP framing, and every configured low-memory key. 3. MIT and bundled lwIP notice obligations are enumerated and sample binary-distribution notices are generated from the pinned sources. 4. Apple provider and harness build risks, global state, threading model, allocator hooks, shutdown contract, and known patches are documented. 5. The baseline declares unmodified upstream as default and defines the evidence required before any fork.","assignee":"","blockedBy":[],"blocks":["TASK-260715-p89bdj","TASK-260715-1vv52g"],"checklist":[{"text":"Exact HEV, core, task-system, and lwIP revisions and hashes are pinned","done":false},{"text":"Descriptor, framing, configuration, lifecycle, and license claims are source-backed","done":false},{"text":"The manifest and notice audit are attached as TASK-ID-scoped outcomes","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:01:34Z","description":"Establish the exact upstream HEV dependency set used by the M0 bridge spike and verify its Apple build, descriptor contract, UDP-in-TCP framing, configuration keys, licenses, notices, and fork baseline from primary source.","id":"TASK-260715-uopycx","isBlocked":false,"name":"pin-and-audit-hev-lwip-baseline","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-jnpbyz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: hev-socks5-tunnel, hev-socks5-core, hev-task-system, bundled lwIP, exact commits and submodules, source hashes, Apple build instructions, descriptor ownership, Darwin family header behavior, socks5.udp tcp mode, low-memory settings, licenses, notices, and upstream issue or patch inventory. Out of scope: modifying upstream, implementing the bridge, selecting production performance constants, or accepting an unpinned release tag.","status":"backlog","title":"Pin and audit the HEV and lwIP baseline","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:28Z"}]
.task-board/.resources/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:9851:[{"ac":"1. The adapter satisfies every compile-time conformance requirement and exposes no ReluxNIOSSH type across the shared transport boundary. 2. Host-key material reaches policy before authentication acceptance and first-use, match, rejection, and change smoke paths are observable. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec channels support bounded writes, reads, EOF, half-close, cancellation, and independent close with configurable receive windows. 4. Byte and time rekey thresholds, server requests, keepalive, connection and channel metrics, and privacy-safe errors are wired to the common schema. 5. The adapter builds and smoke-connects in macOS harness, macOS provider, iOS simulator, and Gate P0 iPhone configurations with pinned dependency evidence.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-nzdzv3","TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-1g9cyt","TASK-260715-pmww4f"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-3ikonq"],"checklist":[{"text":"Adapter fully conforms without leaking candidate types","done":false},{"text":"Host key, channels, windows, rekey, cancellation, and metrics are wired","done":false},{"text":"Apple-target and harness build or smoke evidence is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:15Z","description":"Implement the candidate adapter behind the common SSH transport contract and build it through the generated native and Swift dependency seams in the macOS harness and both Apple provider configurations.","id":"TASK-260715-1af33i","isBlocked":true,"name":"integrate-reluxniossh-candidate-adapter","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: pinned fork dependency; client bootstrap; raw host-key callback; approved public-key authentication; direct-tcpip; bidirectional exec; bounded async reads and writes; per-channel windows; automatic and explicit rekey; keepalive; cancellation; metrics; error mapping; harness registration; iOS and macOS compile and smoke paths. Out of scope: selecting NIOSSH, production lane scheduler, relay protocol, SFTP, password prompts, ProxyJump, agent forwarding, and candidate-specific types outside the adapter module.","status":"backlog","title":"Integrate the ReluxNIOSSH candidate adapter","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped ADR maps every required gate to row-level evidence for both candidates and marks pass, fail, or not run with reason. 2. The selected engine passes every mandatory gate, including Apple targets, pre-auth host evidence, approved auth, hundreds of direct channels, long-lived exec, configurable windows, client and server rekey, real relux compatibility, extension memory, and leak-free lifecycle. 3. A red preferred candidate routes selection to the alternate or returns the story to analysis; no threshold is weakened after results are known. 4. The ADR records exact dependency pins, adapter boundary, approved algorithms, initial window and rekey policy ranges, license notices, security monitoring, and fork or upstream-rebase owner. 5. Rejected evidence, residual risks, device and server revalidation triggers, and downstream tasks unblocked for M1 and M2 are explicit.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-1u2vpc","TASK-260715-2xx2tk"],"blocks":[],"checklist":[{"text":"Every mandatory gate maps to evidence for both candidates","done":false},{"text":"The selected engine has no waived red gate","done":false},{"text":"Pins, maintenance obligations, residual risks, and the selection ADR are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:17Z","description":"Select the production SSH engine only from audited build, conformance, functional, compatibility, rekey, scale, lifecycle, and memory evidence. Document the rejected candidate and maintenance obligations without weakening a failed gate.","id":"TASK-260715-1gjxer","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-m0-ssh-engine-selection","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: every M0 SSH gate; candidate versions; Apple integration; host verification; auth and algorithm support; direct-tcpip; exec; windows; rekey; backpressure; cancellation; compatibility; scale; memory; lifecycle; security and license posture; fork and upstream strategy; residual risks; revalidation triggers; downstream readiness. Out of scope: implementing lane scheduling, relay protocol, profile UX, SFTP, ProxyJump, release approval, and selecting a candidate with a waived mandatory gate.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the M0 SSH engine selection","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. The adapter builds from pinned source with the approved crypto backend for macOS harness, macOS provider, iOS simulator, and Gate P0 iPhone configurations and exposes no libssh2 type across the shared boundary. 2. Socket readiness and LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN are integrated without busy spinning or unbounded buffering, with deterministic cancellation and timeout behavior. 3. Raw host-key evidence, public-key auth, direct-tcpip, bidirectional exec, EOF and half-close, keepalive, metrics, and privacy-safe errors conform or are marked red with reproducible evidence. 4. Initial channel window and adjustment control plus client and server rekey behavior are proven through supported APIs or explicitly fail the candidate; no hidden fallback weakens the contract. 5. Repeated connect and cancel smoke runs return sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, and custom allocations to baseline.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k","TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-1g9cyt","TASK-260715-pmww4f"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-1u2vpc"],"checklist":[{"text":"Extension-safe libssh2 adapter and nonblocking integration build reproducibly","done":false},{"text":"Unsupported window or rekey behavior is recorded red rather than bypassed","done":false},{"text":"Harness and Apple-target conformance evidence is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:15Z","description":"Implement the libssh2 candidate behind the common SSH transport contract, including nonblocking socket integration and bounded async adaptation, and build it in the macOS harness and both Apple provider configurations without masking unsupported gates.","id":"TASK-260715-1ozsb6","isBlocked":true,"name":"integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: pinned libssh2 and crypto backend; extension-safe static or source build; session handshake; raw host-key access; approved public-key auth; direct-tcpip; bidirectional exec; custom receive-window experiment; rekey behavior; nonblocking EAGAIN integration; bounded buffers; cancellation; keepalive; metrics; error mapping; allocator hooks where supported; harness registration. Out of scope: patching libssh2 to force a pass without a separate recorded decision, blocking calls on provider executors, SFTP, password prompts, ProxyJump, agent forwarding, production lane scheduling, and candidate types outside the adapter.","status":"backlog","title":"Integrate the libssh2 candidate adapter","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records device, OS, server, source and dependency revisions, crypto backend, algorithms, config, windows, traffic, duration, loss and latency, counters, resources, raw artifact locations, and pass or fail for every row. 2. Raw host-key evidence precedes auth acceptance and Ed25519 plus the approved fallback pass against all in-scope servers, including real relux. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec remain correct under concurrent activity, nonblocking pressure, half-close, reset, cancellation, and provider lifecycle. 4. Window and rekey rows prove the required control through supported behavior or remain explicit red; a safe 5 GiB mixed run verifies content and resource cleanup when the candidate reaches that gate. 5. Any red row remains red, creates or references focused rework, and is not waived because another libssh2 feature passes.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-2ayxqn"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2xx2tk","TASK-260715-1gjxer"],"checklist":[{"text":"Every libssh2 functional, compatibility, Apple, and rekey row has metadata","done":false},{"text":"Window and rekey gaps remain explicit red with reproducible evidence","done":false},{"text":"Safe mixed-traffic and cleanup evidence plus the full matrix are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:16Z","description":"Execute the complete candidate-neutral functional, compatibility, Apple-target, and rekey matrix against the libssh2 adapter and preserve row-level evidence, including explicit red results for unsupported window or rekey control.","id":"TASK-260715-1u2vpc","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-libssh2-functional-and-rekey-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: macOS harness and provider; Gate P0 physical iPhone provider smoke; current OpenSSH Linux and macOS; older profile; real relux host; host verification; Ed25519 and fallback auth; direct-tcpip; exec stdio; 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped BDP window attempts; bounded pressure; client byte and time rekey attempts; server rekey; at least 5 GiB mixed traffic when safe; cancellation and network loss. Out of scope: NIOSSH results, production lane scheduling, SFTP, release distribution, patching the library inside the measurement task, and waiving an unavailable API.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the libssh2 functional and rekey matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped manifest records exact commits, tags where applicable, transitive dependencies, hashes, crypto backend, build flags, upstream URLs, licenses, notices, and inspected source paths. 2. A capability table maps every M0 SSH gate to a public API, internal hook, confirmed absence, or experiment still required for each candidate. 3. The SwiftNIO SSH 16 MiB child-window default and non-public client rekey surface are verified at the pinned source; libssh2 window and rekey behavior is equally source-pinned. 4. Current security advisories, maintenance cadence, extension constraints, threading, allocator, and binary-size risks are recorded. 5. Unknowns become concrete dependent experiments and no candidate is favored by weakening a missing capability.","assignee":"","blockedBy":[],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-nzdzv3","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-39xz9g"],"checklist":[{"text":"Both candidate and transitive revisions, hashes, licenses, and security baselines are pinned","done":false},{"text":"Every M0 gate maps to source evidence or a named experiment","done":false},{"text":"The candidate manifest and capability table are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:14Z","description":"Establish exact source baselines for SwiftNIO SSH and libssh2 and document their current Apple integration, host-key, authentication, channel, window, rekey, cancellation, algorithm, license, security, and maintenance surfaces before candidate work begins.","id":"TASK-260715-28ok1k","isBlocked":false,"name":"pin-and-audit-ssh-engine-candidates","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: the inspected SwiftNIO SSH commit and transitive SwiftNIO pins; a specific libssh2 commit or release and crypto backend; source hashes; licenses and notices; iOS and macOS build support; extension safety; known CVEs and advisories; raw host-key access; auth algorithms; direct-tcpip and exec; initial windows; rekey APIs; thread and allocator model; cancellation; open upstream issues. Out of scope: changing candidate code, selecting the winner, configuring production lanes, SFTP, or accepting marketing claims without source evidence.","status":"backlog","title":"Pin and audit the SSH engine candidates","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:30Z"},{"ac":"1. The same named suite runs against both adapters with candidate selection as data, and every gate has an explicit assertion rather than an informal log check. 2. Host verification tests prove policy sees raw key evidence before authentication acceptance and rejects a changed key without opening destination channels. 3. Channel tests verify independent open, bounded write, read, EOF, half-close, reset, cancel, close, and per-channel windows under concurrent activity. 4. Fake-clock and byte-count tests trigger client rekey; fixture-driven tests cover server rekey and active channels across key exchange. 5. Repeated cancellation at connection and channel states returns task, channel, socket, and descriptor counts to baseline and metrics use the common schema.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-39xz9g"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-1u2vpc"],"checklist":[{"text":"One candidate-neutral Swift Testing suite asserts every functional gate","done":false},{"text":"Host policy, windows, rekey, backpressure, and cancellation are deterministic","done":false},{"text":"Test inventory and passing or red candidate evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:16Z","description":"Implement one Swift Testing and harness suite that runs unchanged against both candidate adapters and verifies host policy, auth, channel semantics, exec, windows, rekey, backpressure, cancellation, metrics, and resource cleanup.","id":"TASK-260715-2d3g5e","isBlocked":true,"name":"add-common-ssh-transport-conformance-tests","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: fake-clock and deterministic socket or server fixtures; host-key first use, match, change, and rejection; Ed25519 and fallback auth; direct-tcpip and exec; concurrent channels; bounded write pressure; EOF, half-close, reset, and early close; window profiles; client byte and time rekey; server rekey; keepalive; cancellation at each state; metrics and descriptor baselines. Out of scope: candidate-specific pass exceptions, production lane scheduling, full physical performance matrix, relay framing, UI, and tests that rely only on sleeps.","status":"backlog","title":"Add common SSH transport conformance tests","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped contract defines every operation, state transition, cancellation point, timeout, ownership boundary, error, metric, and privacy rule required by the M0 matrix. 2. Host-key bytes, algorithm, and fingerprint evidence are available to policy before authentication acceptance, including first-use, match, and change cases. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec channels have explicit open, bounded write, read, EOF, half-close, reset, cancel, and close semantics. 4. Window policy, WINDOW_ADJUST, automatic byte and time rekey, explicit test trigger, server rekey, keepalive, and key-exchange channel behavior are independently observable. 5. The conformance contract can be implemented by either candidate without exposing candidate types to ReluxTunnelCore consumers.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-nzdzv3","TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-2d3g5e"],"checklist":[{"text":"Candidate-neutral channel, lifecycle, error, and metric semantics are exact","done":false},{"text":"Host verification, windows, rekey, and bounded backpressure are independently testable","done":false},{"text":"The reviewed conformance contract is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:14Z","description":"Translate the SSH transport specification into a candidate-neutral implementation and test contract for connection, host verification, authentication, direct-tcpip, exec, windows, rekey, backpressure, cancellation, metrics, and lifecycle.","id":"TASK-260715-2ny6z4","isBlocked":true,"name":"record-ssh-transport-conformance-contract","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: Swift async interface and state ownership; raw host-key evidence before acceptance; supported auth outcomes; destination and originator endpoints; byte-channel and exec semantics; bounded write contract; half-close; per-channel receive windows and adjustment; client byte and time rekey; server rekey; keepalive; cancellation; error taxonomy; metric schema; lane identity for experiments; dependency injection. Out of scope: choosing a candidate, production lane scheduling, flow migration, SFTP, ProxyJump, interactive UI, relay framing, and final window constants.","status":"backlog","title":"Record the SSH transport conformance contract","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:30Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped comparative matrix records identical fixture, device, OS, source, dependency, algorithm, traffic, window, connection-count, loss, duration, and measurement inputs for both candidates. 2. Staged channel counts stop at each candidate safe ceiling with explicit reason; hundreds of independent channels must pass for a selectable candidate. 3. One, two, and four connection trials report throughput, latency, CPU, physical footprint and peak, available-memory samples, queued bytes, window credit, channels, tasks, sockets, descriptors, and failures. 4. At least one hundred connect, active-traffic, cancel, and close cycles show no monotonic resource growth for a selectable candidate. 5. The report estimates remaining extension budget after HEV and bridge baselines, distinguishes reserved window credit from measured allocation, and preserves all red lifecycle or memory rows.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-1u2vpc","TASK-260715-2jatnd"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-1gjxer"],"checklist":[{"text":"Both viable candidates use identical scale and impairment inputs","done":false},{"text":"Hundreds of channels, connection counts, memory, and lifecycle cleanup are evidenced","done":false},{"text":"Comparative raw data and budget analysis are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:17Z","description":"Measure both viable candidates under identical concurrent-channel, connection-count, loss, cancellation, and memory conditions so engine selection accounts for extension budgets and cross-flow behavior rather than functional support alone.","id":"TASK-260715-2xx2tk","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-comparative-ssh-scale-memory-and-lifecycle-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: staged 100, 250, 500, and measured safe channel counts; control-like, ordinary, bulk, early-close, half-close, and idle mixes; one, two, and four independent SSH connections; 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped BDP windows; Wi-Fi-like latency and loss; connection and control-lane failure simulation; repeated connect and close; physical iPhone and Mac footprint; CPU; queued bytes; descriptors; tasks; custom allocator metrics where available. Out of scope: production lane scheduler, flow migration, QUIC policy, forcing a functionally red candidate through unsafe scale tests, and claiming advertised windows are eagerly allocated.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the comparative SSH scale, memory, and lifecycle matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped fixture manifest records server OS and OpenSSH versions, configurations, algorithms, host-key fingerprints, user-key types, destination services, traffic seeds, network profiles, and reproduction or teardown steps. 2. Current Linux, current macOS, one approved older compatibility profile, and the real relux host are reachable through least-privilege test identities. 3. Fixtures deterministically produce success, host-key first use, host-key change, auth rejection, channel rejection, early close, half-close, reset, server rekey, latency, loss, and disconnect conditions. 4. A 5 GiB or larger reproducible source and sink verifies byte counts and content hashes without retaining payload. 5. Secrets remain in an approved external store; artifacts contain only public keys, fingerprints, non-secret configuration, and secret-reference names.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2d3g5e"],"checklist":[{"text":"Server, key, algorithm, traffic, and impairment fixtures cover every matrix branch","done":false},{"text":"The real relux host is represented with least-privilege test access","done":false},{"text":"Privacy-safe fixture manifest and teardown evidence are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:15Z","description":"Create the controlled server, key, algorithm, traffic, and network-condition fixtures required to run identical M0 matrices against both candidates, including the real relux server without exposing production credentials.","id":"TASK-260715-39xz9g","isBlocked":true,"name":"provision-reproducible-ssh-matrix-fixtures","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: current OpenSSH Linux and macOS endpoints; documented approved older algorithm profile; Ed25519 host and user keys; approved fallback host and user key types; host-key change fixture; direct-tcpip destinations; long-lived stdio exec echo or sink; at least 5 GiB deterministic traffic; latency and loss controls; early close and reset endpoints; real relux test host access; credential rotation and cleanup. Out of scope: production user data, broad Internet exposure, password or interactive auth, persistent root service, relay implementation, and storing private test credentials in git or board resources.","status":"backlog","title":"Provision reproducible SSH matrix fixtures","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records device, OS, server, source and dependency revisions, algorithms, config, windows, traffic, duration, loss and latency, counters, resources, raw artifact locations, and pass or fail for every required row. 2. Raw host-key evidence precedes auth acceptance and Ed25519 plus the approved fallback pass against all in-scope servers, including real relux. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec remain correct under concurrent activity, pressure, half-close, reset, cancellation, and provider lifecycle. 4. Client byte and time rekeys plus server rekey survive at least 5 GiB of simultaneous direct and exec traffic without corruption, deadlock, or channel leak. 5. Any red row remains red, creates or references focused rework, and is not waived by the candidate implementation team.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-2ayxqn"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-2xx2tk","TASK-260715-1gjxer"],"checklist":[{"text":"Every ReluxNIOSSH functional, compatibility, Apple, and rekey row has metadata","done":false},{"text":"The 5 GiB mixed rekey run verifies hashes and resource cleanup","done":false},{"text":"Red rows are preserved and the full evidence matrix is attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:16Z","description":"Execute the complete candidate-neutral functional, compatibility, Apple-target, and rekey matrix against the ReluxNIOSSH adapter and preserve row-level evidence without treating the existence of the fork as a reason to accept it.","id":"TASK-260715-3ikonq","isBlocked":true,"name":"run-reluxniossh-functional-and-rekey-matrix","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: macOS harness and provider; Gate P0 physical iPhone provider smoke; current OpenSSH Linux and macOS; older profile; real relux host; host verification; Ed25519 and fallback auth; direct-tcpip; exec stdio; 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped BDP windows; bounded pressure; client byte and time rekey; server rekey; at least 5 GiB mixed traffic; cancellation and network loss. Out of scope: libssh2 results, production lane scheduling, SFTP, release distribution, and fixing failures inside the measurement task.","status":"backlog","title":"Run the ReluxNIOSSH functional and rekey matrix","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:31Z"},{"ac":"1. The fork is based on the exact audited commit and each patch maps only to configurable channel windows, automatic client rekey, or tests and documentation for those behaviors. 2. Tests cover 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and larger capped windows, adjustment suppression, byte threshold, time threshold with injected clock, simultaneous threshold requests, active channels during rekey, and server-initiated rekey. 3. Default upstream behavior remains source-compatible unless the adapter opts into Relux policy. 4. A patch manifest, license review, upstream comparison, rebase procedure, conflict test command, and candidate upstreaming plan are attached. 5. No internal test-only symbol is called through reflection or other fragile access from product code.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-28ok1k","TASK-260715-2ny6z4"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-1af33i"],"checklist":[{"text":"Fork patches are minimal and trace only to window and rekey requirements","done":false},{"text":"Deterministic upstream-style tests cover all new policy behavior","done":false},{"text":"Patch manifest, upstream diff, and rebase plan are attached","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T01:03:14Z","description":"Create the smallest upstream-trackable SwiftNIO SSH patch set that makes child-channel receive-window policy configurable and exposes safe automatic client byte and time rekey while preserving server-initiated rekey behavior.","id":"TASK-260715-nzdzv3","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-minimal-reluxniossh-fork","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: fork from the pinned commit; configurable initial child windows and adjustment hooks; automatic byte and elapsed-time thresholds; safe request coalescing and key-exchange state; public or package API needed by the adapter; focused upstream-style tests; commit and patch inventory; notices; upstream tracking and rebase instructions. Out of scope: unrelated refactors, new SSH features, production lane scheduling, changing cryptographic algorithms, hiding failing tests, or retaining patches not required by the two blocked gates.","status":"backlog","title":"Implement the minimal ReluxNIOSSH fork","type":"task","updated":"2026-07-15T01:04:30Z"}]
