.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-34d4du/TASK-260720-34d4du_inputs.md:1:Extend the ReluxNIOSSH fork (Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH, pinned swift-nio-ssh 0.14.1/31cdc3c) with three PUBLIC API surfaces the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6, in Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift) needs for the adapter, discovered by TASK-260715-1af33i (read TASK-260715-1af33i_fork-api-blocker.md for exact upstream line refs). (1) EXTERNAL ASYNC SIGNER: add a public public-key user-auth offer that takes wire-format public key bytes + algorithm and an async signature callback over NIOSSH's constructed auth payload, WITHOUT constructing/holding/exporting a concrete NIOSSHPrivateKey (upstream only offers Offer.privateKey with a concrete key + synchronous internal signing). Private keys must never leave the caller (security-privacy.md). (2) REPLY KEEPALIVE: expose a public reply-observing global-request op (the internal sendGlobalRequestMessage/GlobalRequestMessage) so the adapter can send keepalive@openssh.com with want-reply + bounded payload and measure RTT, preserving packet sequence/encryption/MAC ordering. Do NOT reuse sendTCPForwardingRequest (creates remote listeners). (3) ALGORITHM POLICY + SNAPSHOT: expose caller-configurable KEX + host-key allowlists on the client configuration AND a public immutable snapshot/event of the EXACT negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC (upstream keeps NegotiationResult + host-key accessor internal/test-only). Keep the delta MINIMAL and allowlisted, update PATCH_MANIFEST + delta/rebase docs, preserve Apache-2.0 attribution, keep upstream crypto untouched and the 323 upstream tests green, add deterministic fork tests for each hook. Concrete NIOSSH types stay inside the fork/adapter boundary (ReluxTunnelCore must not import them; make validate-core enforces). If any hook cannot be exposed without a large/unsafe change, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact delta + a viability note for TASK-260715-1gjxer.
