Implemented and handed off to review.

- Added public typed server-KEX lifecycle observation with monotonic generation.
- Added bounded, nonblocking, reply-correlated global requests with RTT and timeout/miss handling.
- Rebuilt the static extension-safe XCFramework reproducibly; notices and checksum gates remain intact.
- Added deterministic C fixture and Swift packaging tests.

Validation passes:

- `make validate-libssh2`
- `make test-libssh2-source-gates`
- Repeated live OpenSSH test: 14 KEX transitions, failure path, 29 ms RTT, timeout/miss
- `make validate-core`: 64 tests plus `swift build`
- Strict Swift formatting and Python validation
- Two byte-identical XCFramework rebuild locks

The broader `make validate-native` was attempted but stops at an unrelated pre-existing HEV macOS 10.14/11.0 minimum-version mismatch before Xcode builds. This is documented in the [task results](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-2sltje/TASK-260720-2sltje_results.md).

Key changes: [fork patch](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/Dependencies/ReluxLibSSH2/patches/0001-public-client-rekey.patch), [integration test](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/Dependencies/ReluxLibSSH2/Tests/rekey_test.c), and [patch manifest](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/Dependencies/ReluxLibSSH2/PATCH_MANIFEST.json).
